{
    if (name != NULL) {
        json_emit_element(json, name);
    }

    qstring_append(json->str, "{ ");

    json->omit_comma = true;
}
```

By adding the check for `name != NULL`, the function ensures that it only attempts to emit the element if `name` is valid, thus preventing potential issues related to `NULL` pointers.

