To fix this vulnerability, the `thread_pool_init_one` function should be modified to handle null pointers. This can be achieved by adding a null check before accessing the pointer.

```c
static void thread_pool_init_one(void *arg1, void *arg2)
{
    if (arg2!= NULL) {
        // Initialize thread pool with arg2
    } else {
        // Handle null pointer error
    }
}
